{{Term/Store|Stall|Stalls|Series, BotW|plural}} are recurring locations in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW}}<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 318}}</ref> Stalls go unnamed in {{TotK}}.

{{TOC|limit= 4}}

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Stalls are the [[General Store]]s located in the center of [[Gerudo Town]]. All of the Stalls are managed by [[Gerudo]] women. According to [[Spera]], many of the Stalls' proprietors are married and live outside of Gerudo Town, but they return to sell their wares.<ref>{{Cite|[Your husband?] Oh, yes. And a newlywed, too! Many of the vendors who work these stalls are married, in fact. It's pretty typical of married vai to live outside these walls, really. But we come back to sell our wares, of course!|Spera|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 137}}</ref>

====Arrow Specialty Shop====
{{Main|Arrow Specialty Shop}}
The [[Arrow Specialty Shop]] is a small [[Arrow]]-based General Store managed by [[Danda]].<ref>{{Cite|As you can see, this is an {{Color BotW|Blue|arrow specialty shop}}.|Danda|BotW}}</ref> Danda sells [[Arrow]]s, [[Fire Arrow]]s, [[Ice Arrow]]s, [[Shock Arrow]]s, and [[Bomb Arrow]]s. At night, Danda's granddaughters, [[Kalani]] and [[Makure]], sleep by her side.<ref>{{Cite|It's dark out now, so I'm going back to my vaba's booth!|Makure|BotW}}</ref>

====Lorn's Fruit Stand====
{{Main|Lorn's Fruit Stand}}
[[Lorn's Fruit Stand]] is a small [[General Store]] in Gerudo Town managed by [[Lorn]]. At night, Lorn's daughter [[Dalia]] sleeps here. [[Emri]], a fellow fruit merchant at the Kara Kara Bazaar, competes with Lorn.<ref>{{Cite|Huh? Oh, vasaaq... I've got plenty of {{Color BotW|Blue|hydromelons}}... I bet more than you'll find in {{Color BotW|Blue|Gerudo Town}}. Why not buy a bunch while you're here?|Emri|BotW}}</ref>

====Ardin's Stall====
[[Ardin]]'s Stall is a [[Mushroom]] General Store. She claims that the Gerudo keep their skin beautiful with the Mushrooms that she sells.<ref>{{Cite|Just between us... The Gerudo keep their skin so beautiful thanks to the mushrooms that grow here.|Ardin|BotW}}</ref> As [[Link]] approaches the Stall, Ardin will greet him.<ref>{{Cite|Vasaaq!|Ardin|BotW}}</ref> When Link makes a purchase, Ardin will thank him and encourage him to use the nearby kitchen for [[Cooking]].<ref>{{Cite|Sarqso! If you want to cook, the kitchen is available for any vai to use. "Any vai," haha! We're all vai here!|Ardin|BotW}}</ref> She also encourages him to eat many Mushrooms so he can grow bigger.<ref>{{Cite|Sarqso! Eat hearty and grow big!|Ardin|BotW}}</ref> If Link buys her entire stock, Ardin claims to be selling Mushrooms that only the beautiful can see.<ref>{{Cite|Myserious mushrooms!|Ardin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Vasaaq! Step right up and sample my wares: rare, mysterious mushrooms, only visible to the eyes of the most beautiful!|Ardin|BotW}}</ref> However, she admits the truth to Link and promises to restock soon.<ref>{{Cite|Oh-it's just you. After you bought all my mushrooms, I had nothing left to restock my stall... But now, I think people will fall for this. I'll make sure to restock my mushrooms. When you have some money to spend, please come back by here.|Ardin|BotW}}</ref>

Both [[Jules]] and [[Nellie]] frequent Ardin's Stall. Jules will weigh the value of [[Chillshroom]]s against a [[Sunshroom]]s in the [[Gerudo Desert]], which features [[Heat]] during the day and [[Freezing Climate]]s at night.<ref>{{Cite|{{Small|{{Color BotW|Blue|Chillshrooms}} are great, but the nights here are so cold... Maybe I should get some {{Color BotW|Blue|sunshrooms}} instead...}}|Jules|BotW}}</ref> She also believes Ardin's claim to be selling Mushrooms only beautiful people can see.<ref>{{Cite|{{Small|Mushrooms that only beautiful people can see... I think...maybe I’m starting to see something?}}|Jules|BotW}}</ref>

When Nellie is at Ardin's Stall, she recalls that her mother used to say that Mushroom dishes were good for dealing with headaches.<ref>{{Cite|My mom often said that dishes with mushrooms were good for nursing serious headaches.|Nellie|BotW}}</ref> As a result, she makes [[Fragrant Mushroom Sauté]] whenever she is tired, which she explains is made with [[Goron Spice]] and Mushrooms.<ref>{{Cite|So...when I'm feeling tired, I always make {{Color BotW|Blue|fragrant mushroom sauté}}. I love that curry flavor! It's a simple dish that you can make if you have some {{Color BotW|Blue|Goron spice}} and {{Color BotW|Blue|mushrooms}}.|Nellie|BotW}}</ref> Initially, she is hesitant to believe Ardin is selling Mushrooms that can only be seen by beautiful people.<ref>{{Cite|Mushrooms that only beautiful people can see? Not like I'll fall for that. Wait, you're not seriously saying you can see them, are you?|Nellie|BotW}}</ref> If Link claims he can see them, Nellie admits that she thought Ardin was lying to her customers while she was out of stock.<ref>{{Cite|[Yup, I can see them.] Oh, wow, really? And I just thought it was all some kind of joke that Ardin came up with to trick her customers when she's all out...|Nellie|BotW}}</ref> While she does not care if she can see them, she claims she would have been able to when she was younger.<ref>{{Cite|Well, I don't care if I can see them or not. I could have seen them when I was younger—that much I know.|Nellie|BotW}}</ref> If Link says that he cannot see them, Nellie confirms that Ardin was telling a lie.<ref>{{Cite|[I can't see them.] Oh, well, if someone as pretty as you can't see them, that means... Then Ardin must have made up another silly lie. She tells really weird ones sometimes.|Nellie|BotW}}</ref>

